  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, far outperforming image-only ResNet50 (config_010) at 20.8%. This establishes RNA as the dominant modality and makes it the priority for improvement. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile (multiple spatial profiles per cell) adds discriminative signal beyond a single profile. This is a foundational design choice that gates many downstream configurations. This experiment (config_002) tests multiprofile + avgpool aggregation with the same PCA n2000 encoder, isolating the effect of multiple profiles with the simplest aggregation. It is the minimal, clean extension of our best result (one conceptual change: single→multiprofile), making the comparison directly interpretable. If multiprofile helps, it justifies investing remaining budget in multiprofile variants (transformer aggregation, learned encoders, multimodal fusion); if it doesn't, we can focus on single-profile encoder improvements. With 7 experiments left, resolving this structural question early maximizes information value for the rest of the search."
}

